---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ProductScreenshot from '../components/ProductScreenshot.astro';
import LaunchStatus from '../components/LaunchStatus.astro';
import { appUrl, siteConfig, siteUrl } from '../lib/site';
const description = 'Find saved phone conversations by caller, date, transcript words, or what you discussed. Understand text search, AI search coverage, and listening back in Callery.';
const schema = [
  { '@type': 'WebPage', name: 'Search inside your call recordings', description, url: siteUrl('/search-call-recordings') },
  { '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [{ '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Callery', item: siteUrl('/') }, { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Search call recordings', item: siteUrl('/search-call-recordings') }] },
];
---
<SiteLayout title="Search Inside Your Call Recordings" description={description} schema={schema}>
  <article class="container reading-page search-page">
    <header class="page-heading"><h1>Find the conversation<br />you remember.</h1><p>You remember the delivery, the appointment, or the promise. Search your saved call recordings, open the conversation, and listen to what was said.</p></header>
    <div class="actions search-actions">{siteConfig.comingSoon ? <LaunchStatus /> : <a class="button" href={appUrl('/signup')}>Start your call archive</a>}<a class="text-link" href={siteConfig.demoUrl}>Watch the demo</a><a class="text-link" href="/self-host">Self-host Callery</a></div>
    <section class="prose"><h2>Start with the person or the date</h2><p>If you know who you called or roughly when, browse by caller and narrow the date range. You can organize and play recordings without transcribing every call.</p><p>This starts with original filenames that Callery recognizes. Copy recordings from an accessible phone folder without renaming them, and check a small import. A generic filename cannot supply caller or historical call-date details that are missing. See <a href="/phone-compatibility">recording setup and filename requirements</a>.</p></section>
    <section class="prose"><h2>Search words from a conversation</h2><p>Add transcripts to the recordings you want to search. Choose <strong>Text</strong> in the recordings workspace and enter a word or phrase you remember. Text search also checks stored caller details and available summaries, so a matching result may come from those fields rather than the spoken words.</p><p>For example, try <strong>delivery</strong>, then open a matching call and read the transcript to check the context. A recording without a transcript can still be found by its saved details, but Callery cannot search untranscribed audio for what was said.</p></section>
    <ProductScreenshot kind="search" wide />
    <section class="prose"><h2>Describe what you talked about</h2><p>When AI search is configured for your instance, choose <strong>AI search</strong> and describe the discussion—for example, <strong>rescheduling a delivery</strong>. It searches indexed transcript passages by meaning, which can help when you do not remember the exact wording.</p><p>AI search needs configured processing services and transcripts that have been indexed. It can return relevant passages from the conversations it covers. Results are suggestions to review against the transcript and original audio, not a guarantee that every relevant call will appear.</p><h3>Check search coverage</h3><p>The workspace shows search coverage so you can see which recordings have indexed transcripts. Recordings still waiting for transcription or indexing are not covered by that search. You can index saved transcripts without transcribing the audio again.</p><p>If AI search cannot use its meaning-search service, Callery may show keyword fallback and explain the mode. Check that message and your coverage before interpreting an empty result as proof that a conversation never happened.</p><p>The screenshot above shows an actual <strong>Text</strong> search with fictional recordings. It does not demonstrate a completed AI search.</p></section>
    <section class="prose"><h2>Read the passage. Return to the audio.</h2><p>Open the matching recording to read the transcript and play the original. Where transcript timing is available, a passage can take you back to its place in the audio. Untimed transcripts do not provide an exact playback position.</p><p>Use summaries to get your bearings, then check important details in the recording itself. Transcription, summaries, and search can make mistakes.</p></section>
    <ProductScreenshot kind="transcript" wide />
    <section class="prose"><h2>Keep years of recordings useful</h2><p>Moving files off a phone should not make the conversations harder to find. Keep an independent backup of the original folder and preserve filenames when copying recordings between phones, computers, or downloaded cloud-storage folders.</p><p>Follow the <a href="/guides/backup-and-organize-android-call-recordings">backup and phone-change guide</a> or read the <a href="/docs/user-guide">Callery user guide</a> for the upload, transcript, and search workflow. Callery does not automatically sync Google Drive or retrieve a dialer’s private recordings.</p></section>
    <aside class="callout"><h2>Bring the originals. Find the details.</h2><p>{siteConfig.comingSoon ? 'Managed Callery is launching soon. Explore the demo or self-host the open-source app today.' : 'Use Callery in your browser, or run the open-source app yourself.'}</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/phone-compatibility">Check your recording setup</a><a class="text-link" href="/self-host">Explore self-hosting</a></div></aside>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
<style>
.search-page>.page-heading h1{max-width:22ch}.search-actions{margin:0 0 38px;gap:20px}.search-actions .text-link{font-size:13px}.search-page>.prose{margin-block:42px}.search-page>.prose h2{font-size:31px}.search-page>.prose h3{margin-top:30px;font-size:23px}.search-page>.prose p{font-size:16px;line-height:1.95}.search-page>.callout{margin-top:45px}.search-page>.callout h2{font-size:28px}.search-page>.callout .text-link{font-size:13px}@media(max-width:760px){.search-page>.prose h2{font-size:27px}.search-page>.prose p{font-size:15px}.search-actions{gap:15px}.search-page>.prose{margin-block:35px}.search-page>.callout h2{font-size:25px}}
</style>
